# Lyra milestone D: native elastic face and procedural head collar.
# The native face, shared eyes and fixed collar inherit the original head hierarchy once.
# Fixed jaw/eyes; bounded smile controls; independent static equilibrium at each clamped time.
# Lyra Procedural NoMesh | fixed-hinge reference choreography
# Metres; +Y up, +Z forward. A() uses degrees. t is seconds, clamped0..15.
# Shapes are analytic native primitives/profiles; no imported surface data.
# Arm: pure shoulder swing/twist, fixed elbow hinge, signed forearm roll,
# pure wrist swing. Original forearm roll cap65deg; wrist axial rotation0.
# Pure swing identity: Ry(-azimuth) Rx(magnitude) Ry(azimuth).
# All motion coordinates use quintic smoother transitions; radius/angle
# parameters preserve the hinge and cone limits throughout every transition.
